sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch14-12> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-12--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-12--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch14-12: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.56" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.558"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.6"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The comparison Thompson makes is a sensitivity calculation: separating leaves along the stem versus adjusting azimuth. Typical internodes, leaf sizes, and divergences are known from many studies, but they are not one downloadable shoot dataset, and the sunflower file does not represent leafy stems. The geometric inequality can be evaluated for published ranges with standard models; the adaptive conclusion that the ideal angle therefore cannot be the plant's means is a further inference." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: In a light-interception model, vary internode length and divergence angle over the ranges seen on leafy shoots and compare the change in mutual shading. The geometric claim is supported if realistic internode changes reduce overlap far more than realistic angle changes; it is refuted if, at observed leaf sizes, angle adjustments move exposure as much as internode changes do." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Divergence angle and internode length are seldom published together as an open shoot-architecture table.", "A larger geometric effect on exposure does not by itself show what the plant's developmental means of optimizing light are." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-12--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of thompson1917-ch14-12 by Grok 4.7: 0.7" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-12--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch14-12> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/thompson1917-ch14-12--grok--operationalizability> .
